# /scripts - Needed for postinstall

# TypeDoc
typedoc.json
docs/api/

# ─── Secrets: never part of the build context ────────────────────────
# Both Dockerfiles run `COPY . .`, and .gitignore does NOT filter a local
# build context — so without these a `docker build` from a configured
# checkout (the prod host, a self-hoster's box, a laptop) copies the live
# .env into the builder layer. Next.js standalone output then copies loaded
# .env files into .next/standalone/, which the runtime stage ships, and
# `cache-to ... mode=max` would also export the builder layer itself to the
# registry cache. CI checkouts carry none of these, so excluding them only
# changes what a local build can leak.
#
# `**/` also matches the context root. The trailing re-include keeps the
# committed template available.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc
!.env.example
**/.npmrc
**/.yarnrc
**/.yarnrc.yml
**/.netrc
**/.pgpass
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.ssh
**/.aws
**/.docker
**/.kube
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
# Local secret directories and the SOPS blob. Root-anchored on purpose:
# `**/secrets` would also drop any source directory that merely has that name.
secrets
.secrets
infra/sops
# Local tool settings can carry tokens (e.g. settings.local.json env blocks).
.claude
.vercel

# ─── Runtime data and dumps: user content, not source ────────────────
# Root-anchored: `**/logs` would drop app/api/agents/[id]/logs/, which is
# a route, not a log directory.
uploads
data
logs
backups
console-log-backup-*
z_reports
memory-bank
coverage
**/*.dump
**/*.sql.gz
**/*.tar.age
